,"material":"steel-desk","role":"detail","tone":0.2,"size":[0.0225,0.045,0.045],"transform":{"translation":[0.3,0.0,0.0]},"member":"column-left","part":"joint"},{"id":"support-contact-foot-left","kind":"box","bone":"foot-left","material":"steel-desk","role":"ground","tone":0.2,"size":[0.12,0.008,0.12],"transform":{"translation":[0.0,0.004,0.0]},"member":"foot-left","part":"support","anchor":"contact-foot-left"},{"id":"j-r-stage","kind":"box","bone":"stage-right","material":"steel-desk","role":"detail","tone":0.2,"size":[0.0225,0.045,0.045],"transform":{"translation":[0.35,0.0,0.0]},"member":"stage-right","part":"joint"},{"id":"j-r-column","kind":"box","bone":"column-right","material":"steel-desk","role":"detail","tone":0.2,"size":[0.0225,0.045,0.045],"transform":{"translation":[0.3,0.0,0.0]},"member":"column-right","part":"joint"},{"id":"support-contact-foot-right","kind":"box","bone":"foot-right","material":"steel-desk","role":"ground","tone":0.2,"size":[0.12,0.008,0.12],"transform":{"translation":[0.0,0.004,0.0]},"member":"foot-right","part":"support","anchor":"contact-foot-right"},{"id":"mass-top","kind":"box","bone":"top","material":"particleboard-laminate","role":"detail","tone":0.4,"size":[0.08,0.025,0.08],"transform":{"translation":[0.55,0.0125,0.0]},"member":"top","part":"mass"}],"decisions":[{"en":"1:50 is the full model: 16 mm foot plates with chamfered ends, three nested hollow telescoping square tubes per side (64, 54 and 44 mm with 4 mm walls, collar ring and top cap), a 90 x 35 x 90 mm column bracket, the 100 x 148 x 100 mm drive housings on steel mounts beside the sleeves, a 25 mm laminated particleboard top with 4 mm rounded edges, a hollow 50 mm steel rail on four mounting pads, the cable tray as a 7.5 mm U channel, the keypad under the front edge, and monitor (base, tapered neck, 40 mm panel with glazed screen) and laptop on the top; the laptop stands on four 8 mm rubber feet (the drawing shows it raised accordingly), so its underside is free air.","de":"1:50 ist das volle Modell: 16 mm Fussplatten mit gefasten Enden, pro Seite drei verschachtelte hohle Teleskop-Vierkantrohre (64, 54 und 44 mm mit 4 mm Wand, Kragenring und Kopfkappe), ein 90 x 35 x 90 mm Säulenwinkel, die 100 x 148 x 100 mm Antriebsgehäuse auf Stahlhaltern neben den Hülsen, eine 25 mm beschichtete Spanplattenplatte mit 4 mm gerundeten Kanten, eine hohle 50 mm Stahlschiene auf vier Montageplatten, die Kabelwanne als 7,5 mm U-Profil, das Bedienfeld unter der Vorderkante sowie Monitor (Fuss, verjüngter Hals, 40 mm Panel mit verglastem Schirm) und Laptop auf der Platte; der Laptop steht auf vier 8 mm Gummifüssen (die Zeichnung zeigt ihn entsprechend angehoben), seine Unterseite liegt also in freier Luft."},{"en":"Thermal and structure reference the body solids, except the top board: its outer shell is a real thermal solid cut into strips (16 at 1:50, 8, 4 and 2 at the coarser scales) because the validator judges burial per mesh face and one 1.6 x 0.8 m face would be buried completely by the laptop or the monitor base standing on it; at 1:50 it is nested (laminate outside, board inside, asset layer order corrected to innermost first). Joints are the slide stages between the telescoping parts, the top mass sits at the top centre of mass, supports are contact pads under the feet.","de":"Thermik und Tragwerk verweisen auf die Körper, ausser bei der Platte: ihre äussere Schale ist ein echter Thermikkörper in Streifen (16 bei 1:50, 8, 4 und 2 bei den gröberen Massstäben), weil der Validator die Überdeckung je Netzfläche beurteilt und eine einzige 1,6 x 0,8 m Fläche vom Laptop oder Monitorfuss darauf vollständig überdeckt würde; bei 1:50 ist sie verschachtelt (Beschichtung aussen, Spanplatte innen, Schichtfolge des Assets auf innen zuerst korrigiert). Gelenke sind die Gleitstufen zwischen den Teleskopteilen, die Masse der Platte sitzt im Schwerpunkt, Auflager sind Kontaktflächen unter den Füssen."}]},"100":{"status":"authored","denominator":100,"body":[